Subject: Getting the Error: All inputs to rbind.fill must be data.frames after upgrade to rmr 3.2
Message-ID: <lPnp1lWgUEU.uObKU8kg33cJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/lPnp1lWgUEU/m/uObKU8kg33cJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I have recently upgraded my RMR version from 3.1 to 3.2 and the leftouterjoin fails with the error Error: All inputs to rbind.fill must be data.frames
It was running fine with RMR version 3.1

My R version is 3.1. It is failing in R 3.0.2 too.

Code snippet for which it is giving me the error.

library(rmr2)
library(rhdfs)
rmr.options(backend = "local")

df1<-data.frame(a=c(1:4),b=c(6:9))
df2<-data.frame(d=c(6:9),e=c(6:9))
input1 <- to.dfs(list(key=df1,val=df2))

df3<-data.frame(a=c(1:3),b=c(6:8))
df4<-data.frame(d=c(1:3),e=c(1:3))
input2 <- to.dfs(list(key=df3,val=df4))

reducer = function(key, left, right) {
    if(!class(right)=="data.frame")
        output.val=left
    else
        output.val=right
    keyval(key,left)
}

output<-equijoin(
    left.input = input1,
    right.input = input2,
    outer = c("left"),
    reduce  = reducer)

From uf933519d8090e287 at groups.google.com  Thu Oct  9 15:05:08 2014
From: uf933519d8090e287 at groups.google.com (Guillaume Fontana)
Date: Thu, 09 Oct 2014 15:05:08 +0000
Subject: Performance issue on a simple mapreduce job
Message-ID: <BitJIZVcxBc.lRq3oGlewn4J@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/BitJIZVcxBc/m/lRq3oGlewn4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I'm having a big performance issue on a simple map reduce job.
I have an hadoop cluster setup with the apache basic distribution with 4 data nodes and rmr2 3.2.0.

Here are the map and reduce functions :

mapper = function(null, line) {
  keyval(paste(line[[1]],line[[2]],line[[4]],sep="."), paste(line[[3]],line[[5]],line[[6]],line[[7]],sep="\t")  )
}

reducer = function(key, val.list) {
  library("data.table")
  library("RJSONIO")
  f = as.data.table(do.call(rbind,strsplit(unlist(val.list),split="\t")))
  f = f[!duplicated(f[,list(V1,V2,V3,V4),]),,]
  keyval(key,toJSON(f))
}

and here is how I launch it :
mapreduce(
  input="gs://av-eu-data/RESEARCH/step1",
  input.format=make.input.format(format="csv", sep = "\t"),
  output="gs://av-eu-data/RESEARCH/step2",
  output.format=make.output.format(format="csv", sep = "\t"),
  map=mapper,
  reduce=reducer,
  backend.parameters = list(hadoop = list(D="io.sort.mb=1000") )
)

The input is around 10 Gb.

When I run this job, the 162 mappers get to the end, but the 16 reducers take hours to finish.

I've been looking on Google, but no one seems to have an issue like this. What am I doing wrong?

Thanks!
Guillaume

